data: {"type": "action", "id": "act4", "icon": "seo", "title": "Calling AEO / SEO Agent", "results": [], "results_units": "Results", "started_at": "2026-08-01T09:00:14.526815Z", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:00:28.120034Z", "input": {"subagent_id": "seo", "message": "Run a deep SEO analysis for DOJO AI (domain: example.com). This is for the CMO-level \"master\" SEO health check, so be comprehensive and rigorous. Cover:\n\n1. **Organic traffic & GSC performance**: traffic trends (GA4 if available), top-performing and declining pages/queries via seo_get_ranked_keywords_gsc, CTR/position trends, any indexing issues (seo_inspect_url_gsc on key pages like homepage, /pricing if it exists).\n2. **Keyword rankings**: current ranked keywords (seo_get_ranked_keywords_universal / gsc), position distribution, keyword gaps vs. category terms like \"marketing intelligence platform\", \"marketing operating system\", \"AI marketing platform\", \"marketing automation software\" (these are known buyer-language categories for DOJO — check current rank vs 3-6 months ago if data allows).\n3. **Technical SEO**: Core Web Vitals (seo_get_core_web_vitals) for homepage and 2-3 key pages, plus a deep page-speed audit (seo_audit_page_speed) on the homepage.\n4. **Backlink profile**: seo_get_backlink_summary, seo_get_referring_domains (top domains, authority), seo_get_backlink_velocity (trend last 6-12 months), and identify backlink competitors (seo_get_backlink_competitors) plus a link-gap analysis (seo_get_link_gap) against 2-3 known competitors in the AI marketing platform / marketing OS space if you can identify them.\n5. **Content/keyword gap analysis**: where DOJO ranks vs. where the converting buyer-language categories are (known internal finding: DOJO ranks ~pos 5-6 for \"marketing OS/operating system\" organically but that category converts poorly in paid; the converting category \"marketing intelligence platform\" has near-zero organic presence — please verify if this is still the case with fresh data).\n\nKnown context to ground your analysis (from internal prior research, verify freshness where possible, don't just repeat as fact):\n- Homepage headline is \"The intelligent marketing system\" \n- Internal jargon on homepage: \"compounding intelligence\", \"living graph\", \"proactive agents\" — these have zero buyer search presence\n- Prior finding (June 2026): DOJO ranks organically for \"marketing OS\" (~pos 5-6) but near-zero for \"marketing intelligence platform\" (the higher-converting category)\n\nDeliverable: a structured findings summary with concrete numbers/data points from your tool calls (cite what each figure came from), prioritized issues (P0/P1/P2 style), and clear recommendations. Do not invent figures — if a tool doesn't return data, flag it as a gap."}, "kind": "agent", "scope_id": "s1"}

event: final
data: {"type": "action", "id": "act4", "icon": "seo", "title": "Called AEO / SEO Agent", "results": [{"icon": "", "title": "Result"}], "results_units": "Results", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:03:27.971086Z", "output": "{\"message\": \"# DOJO AI (example.com) \\u2014 Master SEO Health Check\\n**Date of analysis: 2026-07-30 | Market/language scope: US / English (en-US) unless noted**\\n\\n## 0. Data-access caveat (read first)\\n\\n**GSC is completely inaccessible for query-level data \\u2014 confirmed again today.** `seo_get_ranked_keywords_gsc` and `seo_inspect_url_gsc` reject each other's \\\"available\\\" property in a circular loop (`sc-domain:example.com` vs `https://www.example.com/`), a fault first logged 2026-07-24, reconfirmed 2026-07-28, and reconfirmed again just now (2026-07-30) \\u2014 three checks over a week, identical failure. This is a backend property-verification fault, not a formatting issue, and won't self-resolve by retrying. I've logged this in `/shared/Instructions/Topics/SEO.md`. **Action needed: a human with GSC admin access must fix property verification.** Until then, this report substitutes GA4 (session-level, directional only) and third-party estimated data (Moz/DataForSEO via the universal tools) \\u2014 **these are not equivalent to real GSC clicks/impressions/CTR/position, and I have not fabricated any GSC figures.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Organic traffic & indexing\\n\\n### GA4 traffic mix (Jan 1 \\u2013 Jul 29, 2026, 210 days, property `properties/450159275`, registered under domain `example.com` \\u2014 note this domain mismatch itself, flagged below as P1)\\n\\n| Channel | Sessions | Pageviews | Engagement rate |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Direct | 20,294 | 25,180 | 43.0% |\\n| Organic Search | 15,556 | 20,053 | 56.0% |\\n| Paid Search | 5,631 | 7,721 | 69.1% |\\n| Paid Social | 3,847 | 5,880 | 36.2% |\\n| Organic Social | 2,268 | 3,312 | 55.5% |\\n| Referral | 2,056 | 2,912 | 49.7% |\\n| Unassigned | 1,535 | 1,734 | 40.7% |\\n| Email | 827 | 923 | 78.2% |\\n| Display | 369 | 469 | 87.5% |\\n\\nOrganic Search is the #2 channel by volume (behind Direct) at ~74 sessions/day average over the period \\u2014 a reasonable base, but with **zero revenue/purchase events tracked in GA4** (all `total_revenue`/`n_purchases` = 0), so I cannot tie any of this to pipeline \\u2014 flag as a measurement gap, not a traffic problem.\\n\\n**Daily trend (all channels combined, since GA4 doesn't let me isolate organic by day and dimension simultaneously):** sessions ran ~300\\u2013650/day through May\\u2013mid-June, dropped to a ~100\\u2013200/day band through late June, and fell further to a ~20\\u2013100/day band for most of July, including several days under 30 sessions (e.g., Jul 24: 28, Jul 25: 22, Jul 28: 23). This is a **material, unexplained drop in overall site sessions over the past ~5-6 weeks.** I could not confirm whether this is organic-specific (GSC being down blocks position/CTR diagnosis) \\u2014 **P0 gap: someone needs to pull organic-only daily trend and cross-check against any site changes (the homepage's `Last-Modified` header shows content was republished today, 2026-07-30, so the site is being actively edited).**\\n\\n### Indexing status\\n`seo_inspect_url_gsc` on the homepage failed with the same property error above \\u2014 **indexing status of the homepage could not be verified.** No standalone `/pricing` page exists: `https://www.example.com/pricing` 308-redirects to `https://www.example.com/#pricing` (an anchor on the homepage, confirmed via direct fetch), so there's no separate pricing URL to inspect or optimize independently \\u2014 pricing content lives entirely on-page on the homepage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Keyword rankings & position distribution\\n\\nSource: `seo_get_ranked_keywords_universal` (Moz-based estimate, since GSC is down) + `seo_get_domain_traffic_metrics_universal`.\\n\\n**Position distribution across 128 tracked SERPs (example.com, US/en):**\\n\\n| Position band | # keywords |\\n|---|---|\\n| #1 | 3 |\\n| #2\\u20133 | 2 |\\n| #4\\u201310 | 7 |\\n| #11\\u201320 | 29 |\\n| #21\\u201330 | 16 |\\n| #31\\u201340 | 14 |\\n| #41\\u201350 | 23 |\\n| #51\\u2013100 | 34 |\\n\\nEstimated organic traffic volume: **~411 visits/mo** (third-party estimate), estimated paid-traffic-equivalent value ~$3,728/mo. Zero paid keyword presence detected by this tool (contradicts GA4's Paid Search channel data \\u2014 likely a tool/attribution-window mismatch; don't reconcile these two numbers).\\n\\n**The ranking keyword list is dominated by noise, not demand:** of the ~74 keywords returned, most are brand-confusion/typo terms with near-zero volume \\u2014 \\\"dojomojo\\\" (103 vol, unrelated brand), \\\"jodai\\\" (16 vol, typo), \\\"chatbot dojo,\\\" \\\"dojo smart home,\\\" \\\"dojo hosting\\\" (all unrelated third-party \\\"dojo\\\" brands DOJO AI is accidentally competing with in the SERP). Only a handful of keywords carry real commercial-buyer intent and volume:\\n\\n| Keyword | Rank | Volume (Moz) | Ranking page |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| marketing os | 2 | 26 | /blog/what-is-a-marketing-operating-system... |\\n| mql to sql conversion rate | 25 | 60 | /blog/mql-to-sql-conversion... |\\n| ai-first marketing strategy | 23 | 69 | /blog/ai-first-marketing-team-structure-guide-2025 |\\n| dojo software | 29 | 67 | / (homepage) |\\n| chatgpt prompts for referral program strategies | 31 | 66 | /blog/chatgpt-prompts-for-marketing-challenger-brands |\\n\\n**\\\"marketing intelligence platform\\\" does not appear anywhere in the ranked-keyword list at all.** \\\"AI marketing platform\\\" and \\\"marketing automation software\\\" are also completely absent.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Verifying the June 2026 internal finding: still true, confirmed with fresh grounded data\\n\\nGrounded via `seo_get_keyword_metrics` (Google, US/en, DataForSEO) \\u2014 real demand and difficulty, not estimates:\\n\\n| Category term | Search volume (US, monthly) | Keyword difficulty | Intent | DOJO's current organic rank | AI-engine search volume* |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **marketing intelligence platform** | 260 | 18 (low) | Commercial | **Not ranking** (absent from top ~100 tracked results) | 12/mo |\\n| marketing operating system | 30 | 0 (essentially open) | Commercial | Ranks via \\\"marketing os\\\" variant at pos. 2 (blog page) | 41/mo |\\n| AI marketing platform | 1,600 | 80 (very hard) | Commercial | Not ranking | 62/mo |\\n| marketing automation software | 2,400 | 34 (moderate) | Commercial | Not ranking | 24/mo |\\n| intelligent marketing system (DOJO's own headline phrase) | 10 | 4 | Commercial | Ranks #1 (own brand page, near-zero external demand) | \\u2014 |\\n\\n*AI Answer Engine inferred search volume via `aeo_get_keyword_ai_search_volume`, US/en.\\n\\n**Verdict: the prior finding holds and is now grounded, not repeated on faith.**\\n- \\\"Marketing intelligence platform\\\" (260 mo. searches, KD 18 \\u2014 the *easiest* of the four category terms to rank for) still has **zero organic presence** for DOJO. This is the highest-opportunity, lowest-difficulty gap on the board.\\n- \\\"Marketing OS\\\" is real but tiny (30 mo. searches) \\u2014 DOJO's pos. ~2 there (per Moz snapshot; the original June finding cited pos. 5-6, likely a different data source/snapshot \\u2014 direction is consistent: DOJO ranks reasonably here) is a rank in a near-empty category.\\n- \\\"AI marketing platform\\\" (1,600/mo, KD 80) is the biggest prize but also the hardest fight \\u2014 not a realistic short-term organic target without a sustained content/backlink campaign.\\n- \\\"Marketing automation software\\\" (2,400/mo, KD 34 \\u2014 moderate difficulty, decent volume) is a second high-value gap DOJO isn't contesting at all, and it's meaningfully easier than \\\"AI marketing platform.\\\"\\n- The homepage's own headline phrase, \\\"intelligent marketing system,\\\" has essentially no market search demand (10/mo) \\u2014 confirms the account's internal finding that homepage language (\\\"compounding intelligence,\\\" \\\"living graph,\\\" \\\"proactive agents\\\") is disconnected from buyer search vocabulary. This matches the existing \\\"Homepage Language Gap\\\" memory finding \\u2014 no need to re-litigate that; treat as reconfirmed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Technical SEO\\n\\n### Core Web Vitals (real-user, mobile, `seo_get_core_web_vitals`, period ending 2026-07-25)\\nOnly origin-level data is available \\u2014 `/pricing` and `/blog` both fell back to origin-level (`origin_fallback: true`), meaning DataForSEO doesn't have enough URL-level traffic to report them separately (consistent with `/pricing` not being a real page).\\n\\n| Metric | Current (p75) | Rating | 6-mo ago (~Feb 2026) |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| LCP | 3,585 ms | **Needs improvement** | 2,979 ms |\\n| INP | 153 ms | Good | n/a (not reported that early) |\\n| CLS | 0.0 | Good | 0.04 |\\n| FCP | 3,037 ms | **Poor** | 1,208 ms |\\n| TTFB | 1,267 ms | **Needs improvement** | 631 ms |\\n\\n**LCP, FCP, and TTFB have all roughly doubled since ~mid-June 2026** (the history shows a sharp step-change around the week of 2026-06-20, from FCP ~1,643ms to 2,650ms, and holding elevated since). This lines up suspiciously with the GA4 traffic decline window noted in \\u00a71 \\u2014 **worth investigating together: something shipped to the site in mid-to-late June that both slowed it down and may be depressing traffic.**\\n\\n### Lighthouse deep audit, homepage, mobile (`seo_audit_page_speed`)\\n- **Performance score: 56/100** (mobile) \\u2014 below a healthy threshold (70+).\\n- Lab LCP: **13,380 ms** (lab conditions are stricter/simulated-throttled than field data, but this is a severe outlier vs. the field p75 of 3,585ms \\u2014 indicates the page is very sensitive to network/CPU conditions).\\n- Speed Index: 20,106 ms; TTI: 13,470 ms.\\n- Top fix opportunities: **image delivery** (656 KiB, ~2.55s potential savings), **unused JavaScript** (226 KiB, ~1.35s savings), long main-thread tasks (4 found).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Backlink profile\\n\\n### Summary (`seo_get_backlink_summary`, hybrid data source)\\n- Domain Authority: **27** (DataForSEO rank 28), Spam Score: 11 (low-moderate, acceptable)\\n- 390 backlinks, 250 referring domains, 241 referring main domains, 1 broken backlink\\n- First backlink seen: 2023-10-14\\n\\n### Velocity (`seo_get_backlink_velocity`, monthly, w/ absolute totals)\\nClear, healthy acceleration: referring domains grew from 15 (Jan 2025) \\u2192 213 (Jun 2026), with the steepest growth **April\\u2013June 2026** (+46, +49, +44 new referring domains/month respectively) \\u2014 this coincides with the ~$6M seed raise press coverage (Apr 2026). July 2026 shows deceleration (17 new referring domains, 4 lost) \\u2014 the PR-driven spike is fading and needs a follow-up link strategy to sustain momentum.\\n\\n### Top referring domains (`seo_get_referring_domains`, by rank)\\nDominated by PR-wire and startup-news placements from the funding announcement: accessnewswire.com (rank 18), martechtherapy.com (rank 11, spam score 20 \\u2014 worth a quality check), pr.report (rank 8), itjobs.pt, fundz.net, thecmocircle.com, thesaasnews.com. **No links yet from tier-1 martech media (MarTech.org, Search Engine Land, CMSWire) despite those outlets showing up as backlink-competitor overlap domains** \\u2014 see below.\\n\\n### Backlink competitors (`seo_get_backlink_competitors`)\\nSites sharing DOJO's link neighborhood are mostly **PR distribution/wire services** (xpr.media, pr.report, accessnewswire.com) rather than product competitors \\u2014 expected for a young, PR-driven link profile, but it means DOJO's current backlink strategy is \\\"announcement-driven,\\\" not \\\"content/authority-driven.\\\" Real martech-relevant overlaps worth pursuing: **searchengineland.com, cmswire.com, digitalagencynetwork.com, crunchbase.com** (intersections 14\\u201319) \\u2014 these are legitimate targets for guest content/PR follow-up.\\n\\n### Link-gap vs. named competitors (Jasper, Copy.ai, axy.digital)\\nPer press coverage (`contentgrip.com`, confirmed via web search), DOJO's own funding announcement named **Jasper, HubSpot, and Copy.ai** as comparison points; **axy.digital** was independently found positioning itself as a \\\"DOJO AI alternative\\\" for GEO/AEO. Caveat: Jasper (34,621 referring domains, DA-equivalent much higher) and Copy.ai (25,378 referring domains) are horizontal AI-writing platforms at massive scale \\u2014 not apples-to-apples competitors for a marketing-intelligence-OS positioning, so the link gap here mostly surfaces **generic \\\"AI tools directory\\\" sites** (toolify.ai, aitoolsatlas.ai, n8n.io, eesel.ai) rather than martech-specific authority sites. axy.digital itself is tiny (2 referring domains) \\u2014 not a meaningful backlink benchmark. **This is a genuine gap in the analysis: DOJO doesn't have well-matched, similarly-sized organic/backlink competitors identified yet \\u2014 recommend the CMO confirm 2\\u20133 real head-to-head competitors (e.g., other marketing-intelligence or brand-tracking platforms at similar stage) for a proper link-gap and rank-gap analysis next round.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Prioritized findings & recommendations\\n\\n**P0 \\u2014 Fix now**\\n1. **GSC access is broken and has been for a week+ (three independent checks).** Blocks real click/impression/position/CTR data and URL indexing diagnostics for every future SEO deliverable. \\u2192 Escalate to whoever holds GSC admin for example.com/example.com; the domain-mismatch clue (GA4 property registered under `example.com`, not `example.com`) is the most likely root cause \\u2014 check which domain is actually verified with API access in GSC admin.\\n2. **Core Web Vitals regressed sharply in mid-to-late June 2026** (LCP/FCP/TTFB roughly doubled) at the same time overall GA4 sessions dropped ~60-80%. Investigate what shipped to the site around 2026-06-20\\u201327; fix image delivery (656 KiB) and unused JS (226 KiB) per the Lighthouse audit \\u2014 mobile performance score is 56/100.\\n3. **\\\"Marketing intelligence platform\\\" \\u2014 260 mo. searches, KD 18, commercial intent, zero organic presence.** This is the single best-documented, lowest-effort SEO opportunity on the account: real demand, low competition, and DOJO has no content targeting it at all. Build a dedicated pillar page/guide targeting this exact phrase (not just \\\"marketing OS,\\\" which is 8x smaller in volume).\\n\\n**P1 \\u2014 Fix this quarter**\\n4. Homepage jargon (\\\"compounding intelligence,\\\" \\\"living graph,\\\" \\\"proactive agents\\\") continues to carry ~0 buyer search volume, confirmed again via keyword metrics on the closest phrase, \\\"intelligent marketing system\\\" (10 mo. searches). Reconciles with the existing Homepage Language Gap finding in memory \\u2014 prioritize the copy fix already recommended there.\\n5. **\\\"Marketing automation software\\\"** (2,400 mo. searches, KD 34 \\u2014 moderate) is a second real, currently-uncontested category gap; less crowded than \\\"AI marketing platform\\\" (KD 80) and worth a dedicated content play before attempting the harder term.\\n6. Backlink growth is PR-announcement-driven and decelerating (new referring domains: 46\\u219249\\u219244\\u219217 Apr\\u2013Jul 2026). Diversify beyond wire-service placements \\u2014 pursue searchengineland.com, cmswire.com, digitalagencynetwork.com (identified overlap domains) via guest content/PR, not just funding-announcement syndication.\\n7. Confirm 2-3 real, comparably-sized head-to-head competitors (Jasper/Copy.ai are not good comparables \\u2014 they're horizontal AI writing tools 100x DOJO's link profile) to run a proper link-gap and keyword-gap analysis.\\n\\n**P2 \\u2014 Monitor / lower urgency**\\n8. Domain Authority 27, spam score 11 \\u2014 healthy for a 2-year-old domain with a recent PR spike; no red flags, just needs sustained (not just PR-driven) link building.\\n9. GA4 shows zero revenue/purchase tracking \\u2014 can't tie organic traffic to pipeline; flag to whoever owns GA4 conversion/e-commerce setup (outside SEO scope, but blocks any future ROI-based SEO prioritization).\\n10. Several ranked keywords are pure noise (brand confusion with unrelated \\\"dojo\\\" products \\u2014 DojoMojo, dojo smart-home hub, etc.). Not actionable, just be aware these inflate the raw \\\"keywords ranked\\\" count without representing real opportunity.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### What I could not verify (gaps, stated plainly)\\n- Real GSC clicks, impressions, average position, and CTR trends \\u2014 tool inaccessible (see \\u00a70).\\n- Indexing status of the homepage or any other page \\u2014 `seo_inspect_url_gsc` blocked by the same fault.\\n- Whether the traffic decline in \\u00a71 is organic-specific or site-wide (GA4 tooling here can't cross a day-level breakdown with a channel dimension in one call, and GSC is down to cross-check).\\n- A true head-to-head organic/backlink competitor benchmark \\u2014 Jasper/Copy.ai are not comparable in scale; a better-matched competitor set needs to be confirmed with you.\\n\\n### Library changes made\\n- Updated `/shared/Instructions/Topics/SEO.md` with a third dated reconfirmation (2026-07-30) of the persistent GSC property-access fault, including the `example.com` vs `example.com` domain-mismatch lead surfaced again via GA4, and an explicit instruction not to keep re-testing property strings \\u2014 it needs a human fix in GSC admin.\", \"thread_id\": \"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001\"}", "has_succeeded": true, "artifacts": [], "kind": "agent", "scope_id": "s1"}

