data: {"type": "action", "id": "act23", "icon": "file-pen", "title": "Updating SEO", "results": [], "started_at": "2026-08-01T09:01:47.931162Z", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:02:13.269542Z", "input": {"path": "/shared/Instructions/Topics/SEO.md", "old_string": "- Workaround used when GSC is down: GA4 organic-search sessions (`seo_get_traffic_metrics_ga4`, dimension=channel_group) as a directional-only substitute — NOT equivalent to GSC clicks/impressions, do not present as such.\n\n**Reconfirmed 2026-07-28 — still fully broken, same circular contradiction:** `seo_get_ranked_keywords_gsc()` (auto-select) and explicit `sc-domain:example.com` both fail \"not accessible or does not exist.\" `seo_get_ranked_keywords_gsc(property_url=\"https://www.example.com/\")` fails \"not configured for domain example.com; Available: ['sc-domain:example.com']\". `seo_inspect_url_gsc(url=\"https://www.example.com/\")` fails \"Property 'sc-domain:example.com' not accessible. Available: ['https://www.example.com/']\" — i.e. each tool now claims the *other* tool's rejected property is the \"available\" one. Query-level GSC pulls (ranked keywords, indexing inspection) remain completely inaccessible from these tools. Still needs a human with GSC admin access to fix at the property/verification level — not resolvable by retrying strings.", "new_string": "- Workaround used when GSC is down: GA4 organic-search sessions (`seo_get_traffic_metrics_ga4`, dimension=channel_group) as a directional-only substitute — NOT equivalent to GSC clicks/impressions, do not present as such.\n\n**Reconfirmed 2026-07-28 — still fully broken, same circular contradiction:** `seo_get_ranked_keywords_gsc()` (auto-select) and explicit `sc-domain:example.com` both fail \"not accessible or does not exist.\" `seo_get_ranked_keywords_gsc(property_url=\"https://www.example.com/\")` fails \"not configured for domain example.com; Available: ['sc-domain:example.com']\". `seo_inspect_url_gsc(url=\"https://www.example.com/\")` fails \"Property 'sc-domain:example.com' not accessible. Available: ['https://www.example.com/']\" — i.e. each tool now claims the *other* tool's rejected property is the \"available\" one. Query-level GSC pulls (ranked keywords, indexing inspection) remain completely inaccessible from these tools. Still needs a human with GSC admin access to fix at the property/verification level — not resolvable by retrying strings.\n\n**Reconfirmed 2026-07-30 (CMO master SEO health check) — identical failure mode, no change:** `seo_get_ranked_keywords_gsc(property_url=\"sc-domain:example.com\")` → \"not accessible or does not exist\"; `seo_inspect_url_gsc(url=\"https://www.example.com/\")` → \"Property 'sc-domain:example.com' not accessible. Available: ['https://www.example.com/']\". Three consecutive checks across a week now show the exact same circular contradiction. GA4 (`properties/450159275`) confirms the underlying domain mismatch: it reports `domain: example.com` in every row even when queried for example.com traffic. Treat this as a standing, unresolved P0 blocker for any GSC-dependent deliverable until a human fixes property verification in GSC admin — do not keep re-testing property-string variants, it will not self-resolve."}, "kind": "library"}

